    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0930" n="902" sameAs="frus:frus1945-50Intel/pg902"/>

                <head>357. Letter From the Executive Secretary of the Intelligence Survey Group
                    (Blum) to Mathias F. Correa<anchor n="0" xml:id="d357-f1"/></head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1948-12-18">December 18, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mat</hi>: This is merely to tell you that twenty
                    copies of the Survey Group Report were delivered to Mr. Souers this
                        afternoon.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d357-f2"/> I spoke with him yesterday to ask
                    him whether he had decided how to handle the report. He said that he had not yet
                    done so, as he wanted first to see what the report looked like.</p>
                <p>I have not yet shown the report to the Secretary,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d357-f3"/>
                    but will do so shortly. I am sure that the question which still preoccupies him
                    is that of “the man.”<anchor n="3" xml:id="d357-f4"/> In this connection, Souers
                    said yesterday that in his conversations with the President, he (Souers) was
                    taking the position that no move should be made for a change until a suitable
                    successor had been found.</p>
                <p>The report seems to be in good shape and I will keep my ears close to the ground
                    awaiting reactions.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold"> Bob </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d357-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d357-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Central Intelligence Agency Records, Job 86-B00269R, Box 5. No
                    classification marking. The source text is dated December 18, 1949, but from the
                    context this is clearly a typographical error.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d357-f2" n="1" xml:id="d357-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably these were advance copies. The report as finally issued is dated
                    January 1, 1949, on the cover sheet and included a formal letter of transmittal
                    to the NSC dated January 15, 1949. See the source note, <ref target="#d358"
                        >Document 358</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d357-f3" n="2" xml:id="d357-f3-content">
                <p>Secretary of Defense Forrestal.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d357-f4" n="3" xml:id="d357-f4-content">
                <p>Director of Central Intelligence, Admiral Hillenkoetter.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
